+6. **For BI-V150, check the installed CoreX/Triton version and follow local experiment evidence.** CoreX 4.2 examples include repeated [Residual Add RMSNorm forward](wiki/kernels/residual-rmsnorm-bi-v150.md), a separate [two-kernel backward](wiki/kernels/residual-rmsnorm-backward-bi-v150.md), and [GEMM bias epilogue](wiki/kernels/gemm-bias-bi-v150.md); [access](wiki/kernels/affine-access-bi-v150.md) and [scan](wiki/kernels/scan-bi-v150.md) pages retain results and limitations. The [one-layer Megatron GPT experiment](sources/experiments/bi-v150-corex42-stage21.md) separately measures a single FP32 fusion point with synthetic tokens. These results do not establish NVIDIA instruction equivalents or production training speedups. Read `wiki/hardware/bi-v150-stack.md`, `wiki/languages/triton-iluvatar.md`, and `wiki/migration/blackwell-to-bi-v150.md` as needed.
 
 ## Knowledge Base Contents
 
 - Source PR pages, synthesized wiki pages, blog/doc/contest summaries, candidate ledgers, query indices, and artifact bundles.
 - **Verbatim upstream asset bundles** in `artifacts/` (PR patches and complete kernel files or excerpts) — pinned to upstream SHAs via `PROVENANCE.yaml`
+- **Local BI-V150 evidence** in `evidence/` with per-file SHA256 receipts in `sources/experiments/`
 - **Auto-generated query indices** in `queries/`
 - **Controlled vocabulary** (80+ tags) in `data/tags.yaml`, alias map in `data/aliases.yaml`
 - **Hybrid version-claim registry** — per-page `version_sensitive: <id>` pointers + `data/version-claims.yaml` central registry, validated for bidirectional consistency
