rrectness/compatibility under autocast and that throughput did not regress — it does **not** demonstrate optimized BF16 training performance.\\n\\n### Recommendation\\nRetain the verified candidate 0003. Next, collect production training shapes/configurations to extend the tested scope. No optional tuning is warranted beyond the already-met frozen gates.\",\n  \"acceptance_scope\": \"BI-V150, CoreX 4.2.0 / torch 2.4.1 / triton 2.1.0, fixed pinned Megatron local backend (commit 5be9626709af2722333bf54797c954c09edeada3). FP32 residual + RMSNorm fusion only, with residual and weight in float32 and x in {float32, float16, bfloat16}, contiguous 2D/3D tensors with rows<=2048 and hidden<=8192. Representative synthetic GPT training steps (4-layer primary model, 2-layer holdout) with SGD. Throughput measured as complete training-step wall-clock (zero_grad + forward + loss + backward + optimizer.step), excluding data and checkpoint I/O. BF16 autocast accepted only as exact-native-fallback compatibility, not as optimized BF16 training. Three independent processes; promotion gates (geomean>=1.01, holdout/autocast>=0.98, temp-peak-memory regression<=5%) all met.\",\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"The ~1.08% geomean improvement applies only to FP32 residual fusion on the tested synthetic shapes; it is not demonstrated for production shapes.\",\n    \"BF16 autocast passes via exact native fallback (ratio 1.011608); this does NOT demonstrate optimized BF16 / low-precision residual training performance.\",\n    \"16 native-invalid cases per round are CPU-verified compatibility checks (native FP16 RMSNorm backward produces infinities at input scale 0.001) and cannot support any low-precision training claims.\",\n    \"Temporary peak memory equality (0.0 regression) holds only within the specific two-resident-model scope; no single-model total-memory claim is supported.\",\n    \"Standalone GPU event timing can include host launch gaps on the stream; improvement must not be attributed to