+
+# Scope and results
+
+The batch tested algorithmic ideas from the original Hopper/Blackwell technique pages on BI-V150 without relabeling NVIDIA instructions or source measurements. The retained evidence includes every runnable source, raw JSON, console log, failed candidate, SHA256 manifest, and the ixSYS trace failure log. See the repository report `experiments/kernelwiki_iluvatar/PROJECT_REPORT_AND_NEXT_PLAN.md` for the full protocol and interpretation.
+
+The same-tile GEMM+bias epilogue comparison passed FP16/BF16 correctness on three M×N×K shapes, four configurations, and three independent processes per dtype. Selected shape-specific configurations had 1.334× to 3.936× geometric-mean forward speedup versus the *same Triton GEMM tile followed by a separate PyTorch bias add*. The baseline includes an extra launch and is not a vendor optimized GEMM comparison.
+
+An affine FP16 access kernel passed three rounds for contiguous and stride-2 inputs and yielded compiler `n_regs`, `n_spills`, and `shared` metadata. A six-degree Taylor exp approximation passed only the declared [-1,0] FP32 input domain and tolerance, yet did not improve timing reliably. The initial `tl.exp2` variant failed to compile on this Triton build and was retained. A two-pass chunk scan passed correctness but was slower than `torch.cumsum`. `num_stages=1/2/3` and `tl.load` cache modifiers compiled and ran; no NVIDIA-equivalent pipeline or cache behavior was established. FP8 tensors could be allocated, but four FP8 `tl.dot` candidates failed to compile. A fixed-grid persistent add passed correctness but was slower than a regular grid and did not use CLC.
+
+The installed ixSYS 4.2 CLI could not capture a `.ptrace` because the container lacks accessible tracefs/debugfs control nodes and cannot mount them read-write. `stage4-ixsys.log` records this failure; JSON/event samples remain the performance evidence.
