+
+# Scope and results
+
+The recorded run used one of two visible BI-V150 devices. The existing vector-add smoke passed on FP16 input. The repository's basic validation runner then passed all nine FP32 vector-add candidates over lengths 1, 4099, and 1048576, with normal and zero inputs. It passed all nine FP16 GEMM candidates over 64×64×64, 127×65×33, and 256×256×256 after the JIT loop-bound change below. The irregular shape exercises masked tails. The runner also checked PyTorch baselines.
+
+The original GEMM source failed to compile at `triton.cdiv(K, BK)` inside a JIT kernel with `AttributeError: 'int' object has no attribute 'value'`. Replacing the loop bound with `(K + BK - 1) // BK` in an isolated copy made all tested configurations compile and pass the runner's fixed correctness checks. The before and after source files and both reports are retained in `evidence/`.
+
+Timing used five GPU event samples of 20 launches per path. These short measurements establish that timing runs, not stable speed rankings. They do not prove support for BF16, FP8, TMA/TMEM equivalents, asynchronous transfer, training backward passes, or performance portability to other CoreX versions.
