+
+# Scope and results
+
+On one BI-V150 device, a masked BF16 `tl.dot` kernel passed three shapes:
+64×64×64, 127×65×33, and 256×256×256. The test used FP32 accumulation,
+BF16 output, and a CPU FP64 matmul cast to BF16 as reference. The fixed
+atol/rtol were 0.04/0.04. It covers contiguous inputs and one tile shape;
+it does not establish performance, mixed layouts, or exhaustive numeric safety.
+
+A row-wise RMSNorm kernel passed FP16 and BF16 for 3×768, 7×1024, and
+16×4099, including masked tails. The reference computes variance in CPU FP64
+and casts to the output dtype. Checks used atol/rtol 0.02/0.02 for FP16 and
+0.04/0.04 for BF16. All nine fixed cases passed, with five short event samples
+recorded per case. The timing samples are smoke evidence, not stable rankings.
+
+The initial RMSNorm version failed all six cases at compile time because
+`triton.language` lacked `rsqrt` in this vendor Triton 2.1 build. Replacing
+`tl.rsqrt(v)` with `1.0 / tl.sqrt(v)` compiled and passed these cases. The
+initial and corrected JSON reports are retained. The source in `probe.py` is
+the corrected version; `initial.json` retains the original error and original
+source hash.
