+
+# BI-V150 kernel toolchain: observed scope
+
+The `exp-bi-v150-corex42-stage0` Pod exposed two BI-V150 logical devices with 32768 MiB each. Only device 0 was used. `ixsmi` reported driver/IX-ML 4.2.0. In the existing interactive environment, PyTorch 2.4.1 and the CoreX Triton 2.1.0 build compiled and executed FP32 vector add and FP16 `tl.dot` GEMM with masked tails after a JIT loop-bound compatibility fix. These are observations for that Pod and software combination, not general BI-V150 specifications or benchmark recommendations.
+
+FlagOS documents a separate BI-V150 path based on Triton 3.1, CoreX 4.4.0, and PyTorch 2.7.1. Do not merge its version-specific claims with the CoreX 4.2 results. Both paths use Triton syntax; backend support and generated instructions must be checked on each installed build.
+
+## Capability ledger
+
+| Capability | Current evidence |
+|---|---|
+| Device enumeration | Observed on this Pod through PyTorch and `ixsmi` |
+| Triton vector add | Compiled and passed FP16 smoke and FP32 multi-shape checks |
+| Triton FP16 GEMM | Compiled and passed three shapes, including a masked-tail shape, after the loop-bound fix |
+| Triton BF16 GEMM | Three shapes passed fixed checks with FP32 accumulation and BF16 output in the stage-2 probe |
+| FP16/BF16 RMSNorm reduction | Three shapes per dtype passed fixed checks, including a masked tail; forward only |
+| FP16/BF16 Residual Add RMSNorm fusion | Forward and analytical PyTorch backward checks passed on five shapes per dtype in three independent processes; [shape-specific forward measurements](../kernels/residual-rmsnorm-bi-v150.md) compare with unfused PyTorch |
+| FP16/BF16 GEMM bias epilogue | [Three shapes and four tile settings](../kernels/gemm-bias-bi-v150.md) passed three-round checks; same-tile fusion beat a separate PyTorch bias launch in all tested rounds |
+| Chunk scan | Two-pass FP32 `tl.cumsum` prototype passed 4099/65537-element checks but was slower than `torch.cumsum` |
+| Stages and cache syntax | `num_stages=1/2/3` and `tl.load` default/`.ca`/`.cg` compiled and ran in the small probes; target hardware equivalence to NVIDIA mechanisms remains unverified |
+| Staged GEMM compiler IR | `num_stages=2/3` TTGIR contains async slice/commit/wait and uses 2/3 shared buffers; FP16/BF16, two tile and two-shape holdout shows stage-count performance varies and can regress markedly; final machine-instruction equivalence remains unverified |
+| Warp specialization option | Accepted for one 256³ GEMM, but TTGIR/LLVM IR were byte-identical to default; no target role split established |
+| FP8 arithmetic | FP8 e4m3/e5m2 tensors allocated; the four small Triton FP8 `tl.dot` candidates failed to compile in this CoreX 4.2 build |
+| FP8, vendor matrix instructions | Unverified here |
+| TMA, TMEM, CLC, `tcgen05`, `wgmma` equivalents | No verified mapping in this corpus |
+| Repeated forward speed advantage | Observed for the fused Residual Add RMSNorm example against unfused PyTorch on ten dtype/shape cases; no full-training or other-kernel claim |
+
+Use the [retained run reports and source](../../evidence/bi-v150-corex42-stage0/) before citing any observed behavior.
+
+## Native Megatron loop, 2026-10-02
+
+[Stage23](../../sources/experiments/bi-v150-corex42-stage23.md) adds CPU-copy
+numerical verification, real epsilon/dtype semantics, a three-candidate
+Claude Code loop and four-layer complete-step wall measurements. Read the
+[native-backend kernel page](../kernels/residual-rmsnorm-megatron-bi-v150.md)
+for tested scope, autocast native fallback and observed software anomalies.
